# Sobelow scan configuration. `mix sobelow` reads this file automatically, and
# CI passes `--config` explicitly in .github/workflows/security.yml and
# .github/workflows/ci-unified.yml.
#
# `exit:` is why the file exists. Sobelow's default is "None", which makes the
# task halt 0 no matter what it finds (Sobelow.exit_status/2 in v0.16.0).
# Until this file landed, `--config` was a no-op because no .sobelow-conf
# existed, so both jobs above could only fail on a CRASH of the scanner: every
# High, Medium and Low finding reported success. There is no command Sobelow
# accepts that sets a threshold without either this file or an explicit
# `--exit`, and a threshold that lives only in a workflow file is one a local
# `mix sobelow` run does not share.
#
# :medium rather than :low, deliberately. Confidence here is Sobelow's own
# reading of how close a value is to attacker control. Sobelow 0.16 reports
# 259 low findings and 0 medium or high findings after the 13 reviewed skips;
# the low set is almost entirely File operations on paths this terminal
# framework builds itself (config dirs, snapshots, the updater's download
# dir). Reaching :low means pinning 259 fingerprints. A Sobelow fingerprint
# includes the line number, so any edit above one resurrects it and turns the
# gate red for an unrelated reason. A gate that cries wolf on every refactor is
# the gate people switch off. High and medium are the levels where Sobelow
# could not rule out a user-controlled value reaching the sink, and nothing at
# those levels is exempt going forward: the 13 pre-existing high findings are
# pinned individually in `.sobelow-skips`, each with its acceptance reason; a
# fourteenth high finding fails the build.
#
# Raising this to :low is welcome once the low set is triaged. Lowering the
# gate back to "None", dropping `strict:`, or dropping `skip:` silently disarms
# part of it. Strict mode makes an unreadable or unparsable source file a hard
# error instead of scanning the rest of the tree and reporting success.
#
# `skip: true` is what loads `.sobelow-skips`. Without it the fingerprint file
# is inert and the 13 accepted findings fail every run.
[
  exit: :medium,
  strict: true,
  skip: true,
  format: "compact",
  verbose: false
]
